Hello Cliff,

   The only way I can imagine that you can do that without modifying the code is by using, for example, a Gompertz model with bathtub shape and setting the parameter arguments as follows:

   thetaStart = c(-1, 0.1, 0, -10000, 1e-10)
   thetaJump = c(0.01, 0.01, 0, 0, 0)

   This will force the model to set the 'adult' part of the model to 0 as well as the 'c' parameter, and only use the declining Gompertz to fit it. I'm not sure that this will actually work, but you can always give it a try. Still, the latest version of BaSTA should be able to retrieve parameters for a Gompertz with negative senescence. 

   Best,

   Fernando


