Hello Cliff,

   Looking at the life table you sent, although between ages 0 and 4 there seems to be declining mortality, at age 5 all of the remaining 33 individuals die. If there were negative senescence over the entire life course, then a few individuals should have lived much longer, which is not the case. Maybe in this case a better model should be a Gompertz with bathtub shape.

  Best,

  Fernando


